messages.content:
THOUGHT: horizontalFlip currently assumes getCompatibleImage never returns null, but it is annotated @Nullable and other callers check for null. I should mirror that pattern: after creating dimg, add a null check and return the original img if dimg is null, before calling createGraphics. Then I’ll run the Gradle compile to ensure the NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '368,379s/^$/#/;' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/util/Imaging.java && sed -i '368,379s/^/#/' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/util/Imaging.java && sed -i '368,379d' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/util/Imaging.java && sed -i '367a\ \ public static BufferedImage horizontalFlip(final BufferedImage img) {
\ \ \ \ final int w = img.getWidth();
\ \ \ \ final int h = img.getHeight();
\ \ \ \ if (w == 0 || h == 0) {
\ \ \ \ \ \ return img;
\ \ \ \ }

\ \ \ \ final BufferedImage dimg = getCompatibleImage(w, h);
\ \ \ \ if (dimg == null) {
\ \ \ \ \ \ return img;
\ \ \ \ }
\ \ \ \ final Graphics2D g = dimg.createGraphics();
\ \ \ \ g.drawImage(img, 0, 0, w, h, w, 0, 0, h, null);
\ \ \ \ g.dispose();
\ \ \ \ return dimg;
\ \ }
' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/util/Imaging.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

